export const demoPages=[
 {title:'Attention and Learning',subtitle:'A short guide to understanding sequence models',sections:[
 {id:'abstract',heading:'Abstract',zhHeading:'摘要',text:'Attention mechanisms allow a model to focus on relevant information within an input sequence. Instead of treating every word equally, the model assigns different weights to different positions. This short illustrative paper explains the intuition behind attention, outlines a simple experiment, and discusses the limits of interpreting attention weights. It is a learning example, not a published research article.',zh:'注意力機制讓模型專注於輸入序列中相關的資訊。模型不再同等看待每一個單字，而是為不同位置分配不同的權重。這份示範短文說明注意力的直覺概念、概述一個簡單實驗，並討論解讀注意力權重的限制。本文是閱讀練習，並非已發表的研究論文。'},
 {id:'intro',heading:'1    Introduction',zhHeading:'前言',text:'Reading a sentence requires more than recognizing individual words. A reader connects a pronoun to its subject and combines information across distant parts of a sentence. Similarly, a sequence model benefits from a way to retrieve useful context rather than relying on a single compressed representation.',zh:'理解句子不只是辨識個別單字。讀者需要將代名詞連結到它所指涉的主詞，並整合句子中相距較遠的資訊。同樣地，序列模型也需要能夠擷取有用上下文的方法，而不只是依賴單一的壓縮表示。'},
 {id:'intuition',heading:'1.1    The intuition behind attention',zhHeading:'注意力的直覺概念',text:'Consider the sentence: The student opened the book because it was useful. To understand what it refers to, a model can compare the current word with other words. Attention provides a weighted combination of these representations. The weights depend on the query and the available keys, while the values carry the information to be combined.',zh:'想像這個句子：「學生打開那本書，因為它很有用。」為了理解「它」指的是什麼，模型可以比較目前的單字與其他單字。注意力會將這些表示加權組合。權重取決於查詢與可用的鍵，而值則承載要被整合的資訊。'}]},
 {title:'From intuition to an experiment',subtitle:'Method, comparison, and careful interpretation',sections:[
 {id:'method',heading:'2    A simple experiment',zhHeading:'一個簡單實驗',text:'Imagine a controlled comparison between two sequence models. Both receive the same training examples and use the same evaluation set. One model uses a fixed summary of its input; the other can attend to individual input positions. To make the comparison meaningful, the training budget and preprocessing should be kept consistent.',zh:'想像一個受控制的比較實驗：兩個序列模型使用相同的訓練樣本與評估資料集。一個模型使用固定的輸入摘要，另一個則能關注個別輸入位置。為了讓比較有意義，訓練資源與前處理方式應保持一致。'},
 {id:'evaluation',heading:'2.1    What should we measure?',zhHeading:'應該衡量什麼？',text:'Accuracy alone may hide important differences. We should examine performance on longer sentences, record uncertainty across repeated runs, and inspect examples where each model fails. A difference in average performance is more convincing when it is stable across random seeds and relevant to the intended task.',zh:'單看準確率，可能會掩蓋重要差異。我們應檢查模型處理長句的表現、記錄多次執行的變異，並查看各模型失敗的案例。如果平均表現的差异在不同隨機種子下都維持穩定，而且與目標任務相關，結果會更有說服力。'},
 {id:'results',heading:'3    Illustrative observations',zhHeading:'示意觀察',text:'In this example, attention offers a direct route to relevant context. This is a conceptual observation, not a reported empirical result. No dataset, numerical score, or significance test is claimed here. When reading a real paper, locate the experiment and the evidence before accepting a performance claim.',zh:'在這個例子中，注意力提供了一條直接取得相關上下文的途徑。這是概念性觀察，並非實驗結果。本文並未聲稱使用任何資料集、得到任何數值分數，或執行顯著性檢定。閱讀真實論文時，應先找到實驗與證據，再接受效能主張。'}]},
 {title:'Read the evidence, then ask why',subtitle:'Limitations and a reading checklist',sections:[
 {id:'discussion',heading:'4    Discussion and limitations',zhHeading:'討論與限制',text:'An attention weight is not automatically a causal explanation. A high weight shows how a particular computation combines information, but it does not prove that removing a word would change the decision. Interventions and alternative explanations should be considered before interpreting a visualization as evidence of reasoning.',zh:'注意力權重並不自動構成因果解釋。較高的權重呈現某個運算如何組合資訊，但不能證明移除某個單字就會改變決策。在將視覺化結果解讀為推理證據之前，應考慮干預實驗與其他可能解釋。'},
 {id:'questions',heading:'4.1    Questions for the reader',zhHeading:'給讀者的問題',text:'Which assumption is essential to the argument? Are the baselines comparable? Do the conclusions extend beyond the tested setting? Mark the passage that supports each answer, and separate the authors claims from your own interpretation. A useful note should make it easy to return to the evidence.',zh:'哪個假設是論證成立的必要條件？比較基準是否公平？結論是否超出了實際測試的情境？請標記支持每個答案的原文，並區分作者的主張與自己的解讀。好的筆記，應該讓你能輕鬆回到證據所在的位置。'},
 {id:'conclusion',heading:'5    Conclusion',zhHeading:'結論',text:'Attention is a useful way to combine context-dependent information. Understanding its role requires both an intuitive example and a careful look at the evidence. Read for the question, inspect the method, and keep track of what the results actually support.',zh:'注意力是組合依賴上下文資訊的一種有用方法。理解它的作用，需要直覺例子，也需要仔細檢查證據。閱讀時先找出問題，再檢視方法，並持續記錄結果實際支持了哪些主張。'}]}
];
export const glossary={attention:['注意力','依照目前任務，為不同輸入分配權重的機制。'],mechanisms:['機制','讓特定作用得以實現的方法。'],model:['模型','從資料學習規律並產生預測的系統。'],weights:['權重','用來調整不同資訊影響程度的數值。'],sequence:['序列','具有先後順序的一組資料。'],context:['上下文','理解當前內容所需的周圍資訊。'],representation:['表示','用數值或其他形式編碼的資訊。'],query:['查詢','用來尋找相關資訊的表示。'],keys:['鍵','與查詢比較，以決定相關程度。'],values:['值','被權重加總的資訊。'],information:['資訊','模型所處理或整合的內容。'],accuracy:['準確率','正確預測占全部預測的比例。'],evidence:['證據','支持或反駁主張的觀察與結果。'],causal:['因果','涉及原因與結果的關係。'],limitations:['限制','方法或結論的適用範圍。'],learning:['學習','從資料或經驗中調整表示與行為。'],experiment:['實驗','在特定條件下檢驗主張的程序。'],uncertainty:['變異','此處指多次執行時結果的不穩定程度。'],attentionMechanisms:['注意力機制','依照查詢與輸入的關聯，分配權重並整合資訊。']};
